+# WS-10 Implementation Tranche 21 Declaration (2026-04-04)
+
+## Tranche name
+WS_10_IMPLEMENTATION_TRANCHE_21_REMEDIATION_PROGRAM_PHASE_B_AUTHORITY_RESIDENCY
+
+## Objective
+Execute a bounded Phase B authority-residency and parity-hardening kickoff by pinning an authority ownership matrix, wiring enforcement gates, and mirroring minimal status tokens across canonical authority surfaces without altering release-gate truth or claim posture.
+
+## Allowed files
+- formal/docs/release/WS_10_IMPLEMENTATION_TRANCHE_21_DECLARATION_20260404_v0.md (new)
+- formal/docs/release/WS_10_REMEDIATION_EXECUTION_PROGRAM_20260404_v0.md (edit)
+- formal/python/tests/test_ws10_t21_authority_residency_parity_gate.py (new)
+- formal/python/tests/test_ws10_t21_authority_ownership_enforcement_gate.py (new)
+- State_of_the_Theory.md (edit)
+- formal/docs/paper/PHYSICS_ROADMAP_v0.md (edit)
+- GOVERNANCE_VERSION_v2.lock (edit, governance baseline count sync only)
+
+## Out of scope
+- derivation target theorem changes
+- seam status class changes or physics-complete status flips
+- Packet41/Packet42 policy changes
+- scalar freeze policy changes
+- release-gate truth policy changes
+- broad remediation phase expansion beyond authority residency kickoff
+
+## Acceptance
+1. formal/python/tests/test_ws10_t21_authority_residency_parity_gate.py is green.
+2. formal/python/tests/test_ws10_t21_authority_ownership_enforcement_gate.py is green.
+3. Full formal/python/tests suite is green.
+4. ./checkpoint_ladder.ps1 is green end-to-end.
+5. Generated outputs are restored as needed and the working tree is clean afterward.
+
+## Rollback anchor
+269cd81
+
+## Hard stop rule
+If any file outside the Allowed files list changes before acceptance, stop immediately, revert the drift, and treat the tranche as failed until the boundary is restored.
+
+## Boundary freshness note
+This tranche is authority-surface hardening only and intentionally constrained to ownership-residency specification, parity wiring, and gate enforcement for Phase B kickoff.
